{
  "_comment": "Fleet of vulnerable servers across MyGovNet zones. Copy to fleet.json (git-ignored) and fill in. `targets` = the vuln servers you attack; `sources` = tester footholds (local interface IPs) to bind egress from, per zone; `runs` = the zone-to-zone matrix (which source zone attacks which target zones, and the direction). Omit `sources`/`runs` to just run every target from the default route. cloud_ports maps NAT'd SMB/RPC to the forwarded alternates for a cloud target. `appliance` names the security device guarding that leg (Sangfor/Forcepoint/...) so each job's verdicts are device-attributed (recorded as the run's site_id).",
